## Framework-Specific Implementation

According to the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide, for **Vite + React** applications:
- ✅ Use the React-specific import: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- ✅ Add `<SpeedInsights />` component to the main App component
- ✅ Place it where it can track all routes

All requirements have been met correctly.

## Next Steps for Deployment

To start collecting Speed Insights data:

1. **Deploy to Vercel**: Use `vercel deploy` or push to your connected Git repository
2. **Enable Speed Insights**: Go to your Vercel project dashboard → Speed Insights → Click "Enable"
3. **Monitor Data**: After users visit your site, Speed Insights will begin collecting performance metrics

## Technical Notes

- The implementation follows Vercel's official documentation (verified against https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart)
- Speed Insights automatically tracks Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB)
- The script loads asynchronously and won't block page rendering
- Works seamlessly with the project's existing routing (React Router DOM)
- Compatible with the project's lazy loading strategy for route components

